WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.858 --> 00:00:09.375
Press Play to hear the demo groove. Everything runs on your device; nothing is uploaded.

2
00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:15.379
The scope and spectrum analyser show what's coming out.

3
00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:21.254
The rack has eight slots. Each holds a machine modelled on a classic synth or drum machine.

4
00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:25.265
Choose the machine for a slot here: Moog, Prophet, Juno, Jupiter, Virus, Nord, DX7, 303, 808, 909 and more.

5
00:00:25.265 --> 00:00:29.006
Pick a preset. They're grouped by type: bass, leads, pads, strings, keys, bells…

6
00:00:29.006 --> 00:00:39.172
Press ▶ beside the preset to audition it with a phrase that suits it.

7
00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:44.922
Open a slot to see its faceplate: the knobs and switches of the original.

8
00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:59.309
Drag a fader or knob up or down: here the filter frequency, while the groove plays.

9
00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:06.188
Every slot plays through the mixer: level, pan, delay and reverb sends, mute and solo. Nothing to wire.

10
00:01:06.188 --> 00:01:10.762
If you hear nothing, watch the meters here, and check your volume (and on iPhone, the silent switch).

11
00:01:10.762 --> 00:01:18.514
The sequencer: eight tracks of up to 64 steps. Click a step to turn it on or off.

12
00:01:18.514 --> 00:01:23.819
Each track plays one or more slots. The lanes below set notes, velocity, length, chords, slides and CV for patching.

13
00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:32.507
Or draw notes in the piano roll, from C1 to C7. Several notes on one step make a chord.

14
00:01:32.507 --> 00:01:37.615
The patch bay sends LFOs, macros, the mod wheel and sequencer lanes to any knob.

15
00:01:37.615 --> 00:01:42.367
Switch to Graph to see every connection as a modular patch.

16
00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:47.778
Or flip the rack round and plug cables straight into each module's jacks.

17
00:01:47.778 --> 00:01:56.353
Drag from an output to an input. Here the drums' level ducks the chords: sidechain pumping.

18
00:01:56.353 --> 00:02:04.539
Play with the on-screen keys, your computer keyboard (A to K), or a USB or Bluetooth MIDI keyboard.

19
00:02:04.539 --> 00:02:09.426
MIDI learn: press it, click a knob, then turn a knob on your controller. One hardware knob can move many.

20
00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:14.643
Every change can be undone, and your session is saved automatically every ten seconds.

21
00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:25.714
Render to a WAV file, export MIDI, or save into a SoundLab project.

22
00:02:25.715 --> 00:02:32.644
Watch this video again any time from the ⚙ settings button at the top.
